Maybe David's right, but the differences between ( and ) or [ and ]
don't generally get you killed.  To my mind, too, there are too many
things that get you killed which don't make sense in terms of the
simulation.  They only make sense as a test of the attention you
can keep on your keyboard and screen.  Some people like that sort of
challenge, but not me.

Everybody's different, I suppose.  I haven't given it a lot of
thought, but it seems I like the challenge of planning and thinking,
and I'm less interested in the challenge of remembering the character
mapping and noticing and decoding all the information on a computer
screen.  In my mind, I carry an image of a dungeon, and I visualize
and plan in that context.  The details of computer representation
mostly annoy me.


